        "answer": {
          "short": "$ps+qv$.\n\nMultiply along each path ending in $B$, then add the two cases.",
          "worked": "The branches labelled $s$ and $v$ belong to different paths. Include the first-stage probability for each path, then add the mutually exclusive cases.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B\\text{ in the second stage})&=P(AB)+P(BB)\\\\P(B\\text{ in the second stage})&=ps+qv\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
